# Files git never tracks in setdrift-engine. This is the public repo, so the
# rules keep out three things: build output, anything holding data from a real
# cluster, and personal machine or editor state.

# Build output, all rebuilt by `make`.
# bin/: the setdrift and kubectl-setdrift binaries, plus the pinned buf and
# protoc-gen-go tools the Makefile installs there (machine-specific, ~220 MB).
/bin/
# dist/: GoReleaser's output (make release-snapshot, and the release workflow).
/dist/
# A binary built with `go build ./cmd/setdrift` at the root.
/setdrift
/setdrift.exe

# Cluster data. Exports are redacted, but still name clusters, accounts, ARNs
# and hosts, so they stay out of the public repo.
# out/ and setdrift-export/: the export directories the README examples use
# (-o ./out, and the default).
/out/
/setdrift-export/
# Protobuf snapshots (setdrift export --snapshot FILE), wherever they land.
*.pb

# Planning notes kept local for now: the engineering backlog is not public.
/docs/BACKLOG.md

# Go workspace files. The go.work that links this repo to the private one
# lives in the parent folder; this guards against one created here.
go.work
go.work.sum

# Test output: binaries from `go test -c` and coverage profiles.
*.test
coverage.out

# Personal state, never committed.
# macOS folder metadata, at every level.
.DS_Store
# Editors.
.idea/
.vscode/
